<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  CI-ONLY Maven settings for the GitHub Packages publish chain. Passed explicitly with
  `-s .github/maven-ci-settings.xml` by .github/workflows/release.yml and by NOTHING else.

  WHAT THIS METAPOM NEEDS TO RESOLVE
  =================================
  hugmesh-parent is link 2 of 4 (build-config 0.5.0 -> parent 2.8.0 -> commons 2.1.0 ->
  auth-core 2.5.1). Its own <parent> is org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-starter-parent,
  which is on Maven Central. The one net.hugmesh artifact it needs is
  net.hugmesh:hugmesh-build-config, and it needs it on a PLUGIN classpath, not as a project
  dependency: the maven-pmd-plugin / maven-checkstyle-plugin / spotbugs-maven-plugin blocks
  in pom.xml each list it under the plugin's own <dependencies> so the analyser reads the
  curated ruleset (/hugmesh/pmd-ruleset.xml, hugmesh/checkstyle.xml, hugmesh/spotbugs-*.xml)
  off its plugin classloader.

  Maven resolves a PLUGIN's dependencies from the PLUGIN repositories. Those executions are
  bound to `verify`, which runs before `install`/`deploy` even for pom packaging, so a
  settings file with <repositories> only would resolve nothing it needs and die at verify.
  Hence <pluginRepositories>. <repositories> is declared too, for the dependencyManagement
  entry and for any future child-facing use.

  WHY NOT A <repositories> BLOCK IN pom.xml
  =========================================
  maven.pkg.github.com requires authentication even to READ (measured 2026-09-17: 401
  anonymous, and 401 again with a classic token lacking read:packages). This pom is the
  parent of every Java repo in the org, so a repository entry here would make EVERY
  unauthenticated build in the fleet fail — a developer's `./mvnw verify` and
  hugmesh-generator/tests/stack/m2-bootstrap.sh, which is how the compose lane builds these
  libraries and which operator decision 27 deliberately KEEPS as the mechanism.

  AND WHY `github` IS IN HERE TOO
  ===============================
  `-s` REPLACES the user settings file, so the <server id="github"> that
  actions/setup-java writes into ~/.m2/settings.xml is NOT visible to a build run with this
  file. The deploy step's -DaltDeploymentRepository=github::default::... would then upload
  with no credential at all.

  NO SECRET IS COMMITTED HERE. GITHUB_ACTOR and GITHUB_TOKEN are injected by the workflow.

  THE UPSTREAM SERVERS DO NOT USE THE SAME CREDENTIAL AS THE DEPLOY SERVER
  =======================================================================
  `github` (deploy, this repo's own registry) authenticates with the automatic
  ${env.GITHUB_TOKEN}. That is correct and needs nothing from an operator: a workflow may
  always write packages for the repository it runs in.

  The `github-hugmesh-*` servers READ packages published from OTHER repositories, and the
  automatic GITHUB_TOKEN is scoped to the repository whose workflow is running. GitHub does
  not grant it cross-repository package access by default, so the build has to present a
  token that carries read:packages for the owner (the PACKAGES_READ_TOKEN secret). Wiring
  these servers to ${env.GITHUB_TOKEN} would therefore fail as
  `Could not resolve net.hugmesh:...`, the exact string this repo's docs
  teach a reader to interpret as "the upstream is not published yet". That misdiagnosis is
  the cost this split exists to avoid.

  So the read credential is its own env var. release.yml injects
      UPSTREAM_PACKAGES_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.PACKAGES_READ_TOKEN || secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
  which means: use the operator's read:packages PAT if one exists, otherwise fall back to
  the automatic token (the preflight reports when that cannot read the upstream). The
  "Preflight, cross-repo package read" step in release.yml probes the upstream registries
  with this credential BEFORE maven runs, and reports an authorisation failure as an
  authorisation failure. RELEASING.md section 6.2 carries the operator's steps for setting
  PACKAGES_READ_TOKEN. THIS IS NOT VERIFIED. No CI job in this org has ever started (billing).
-->
<settings xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/SETTINGS/1.0.0"
          xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
          xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/SETTINGS/1.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/settings-1.0.0.xsd">

  <servers>
    <server>
      <id>github</id>
      <username>${env.GITHUB_ACTOR}</username>
      <password>${env.GITHUB_TOKEN}</password>
    </server>
    <server>
      <id>github-hugmesh-build-config</id>
      <username>${env.UPSTREAM_PACKAGES_ACTOR}</username>
      <password>${env.UPSTREAM_PACKAGES_TOKEN}</password>
    </server>
  </servers>

  <profiles>
    <profile>
      <id>github-hugmesh-packages</id>
      <repositories>
        <repository>
          <id>github-hugmesh-build-config</id>
          <url>https://maven.pkg.github.com/hugmesh/hugmesh-build-config</url>
          <releases><enabled>true</enabled></releases>
          <snapshots><enabled>false</enabled></snapshots>
        </repository>
      </repositories>
      <pluginRepositories>
        <pluginRepository>
          <id>github-hugmesh-build-config</id>
          <url>https://maven.pkg.github.com/hugmesh/hugmesh-build-config</url>
          <releases><enabled>true</enabled></releases>
          <snapshots><enabled>false</enabled></snapshots>
        </pluginRepository>
      </pluginRepositories>
    </profile>
  </profiles>

  <activeProfiles>
    <activeProfile>github-hugmesh-packages</activeProfile>
  </activeProfiles>
</settings>
